# Built by dot.yaml's go-guarded build step (sp021, dotfiles-ylmp.14): a
# `CGO_ENABLED=0 go build ./cmd/hotkeyd` output, host/arch-specific and
# rebuilt on every `rotz install hotkeyd`. Never commit it -- NO LINKS is
# this dot's whole design (see dot.yaml's header), and a tracked binary here
# would be a second, driftable copy of the daemon sitting next to the source
# that actually defines it.
#
# Anchored (leading slash): matches only hotkeyd/hotkeyd itself, never
# hotkeyd/cmd/hotkeyd/ (the tracked Go source package one level down).
/hotkeyd

# The build's own temp file (dot.yaml builds to this, then renames over
# /hotkeyd) -- normally never left behind, but a killed build can leave one.
.hotkeyd.build.*
